# Project Structure Guide

This is a monorepo project with multiple applications and a shared base package.

## Repository Structure

- **[base/](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/base)**: Contains shared components, layouts, and utilities used across apps
- **[apps/](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/apps)**: Contains individual applications:
  - **[drawing-participation/](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/apps/drawing-participation)**: Main drawing participation app
  - **[restart-ukraine/](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/apps/restart-ukraine)**: Restart Ukraine application
  - **[template/](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/apps/template)**: Template for new applications
  - **[urkrian/](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/apps/urkrian)**: Urkrian application

## Package Management

The project uses Yarn workspaces as defined in [package.json](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/package.json). The workspaces include:
- `base`
- `base/layers/*`
- `apps/*`

## Testing

Testing is done with Vitest and follows a specific structure:
- Test files should be placed in `__test__/` folders
- Component tests should be in `__test__/unit/` with a similar structure to the components
- See [README.md](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/README.md) for more details about testing practices
